    "nome_rls": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Full name of the RLS",
      "title": "Nome Rls"
    },
    "data_completamento_corso": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Date the course was completed or the certificate was issued, ISO 8601 (YYYY-MM-DD)",
      "title": "Data Completamento Corso"
    },
    "scadenza": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Expiry date in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD), only if printed on the document",
      "title": "Scadenza"
    }
  },
  "title": "AttestatoRLSSchema",
  "type": "object"
}

IMPORTANT: All dates MUST be in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD).

IMPORTANT EXTRACTION RULES FOR ATTESTATO RLS:
- 'ragione_sociale': Extract the EMPLOYER company name — the company where the RLS works, NOT the training provider. Look for 'Azienda', 'Datore di lavoro', or 'Mansione: ... - [company]'.
- 'nome_rls': Extract the full name of the RLS who attended the training
- 'scadenza': Extract the expiry/validity date. Look for 'valido fino a', 'scadenza', or compute from issue date + training validity period (usually annual update)

Respond ONLY with the JSON, without additional text.

