You are an expert in extracting data from training certificates (corso di formazione) - various formats from different regional bodies.
Analyze the image and extract the following information in JSON format:
{
  "description": "Schema for training certificates.",
  "properties": {
    "classificazione_automatica": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "boolean"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Whether document was auto-classified",
      "title": "Classificazione Automatica"
    },
    "tipo_rilevato": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Detected document type",
      "title": "Tipo Rilevato"
    },
    "tipologia_corso": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Course type/content - found below title (e.g., 'Addetto ai lavori in quota', 'utilizzo dei DPI di 3\u00b0 categoria')",
      "title": "Tipologia Corso"
    },
    "numero_ore": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Number of training hours",
      "title": "Numero Ore"
    },
    "nome_persona": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Name of the person who attended the course",
      "title": "Nome Persona"
    },
    "data_emissione": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Issue date in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD) - look for 'rilasciato il:' or 'Data,' at the bottom of the certificate",
      "title": "Data Emissione"
    },
    "data_completamento_corso": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Course completion date in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD) - look for 'Periodo di svolgimento del corso', 'Data fine corso', 'completato il'. This is NOT the expiry date.",
      "title": "Data Completamento Corso"
    },
    "data_scadenza": {
      "anyOf": [
        {
          "type": "string"
        },
        {
          "type": "null"
        }
      ],
      "default": null,
      "description": "Expiry date in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD). ONLY fill this if the document explicitly states an expiry \u2014 look for 'valido fino a:', 'scadenza:', 'data di scadenza:'. NEVER use the issue date, the course completion date, or the 'Periodo di svolgimento del corso' as the expiry. If instead it prints a validity period ('Validit\u00e0 5 anni', 'valido 3 anni dalla data di rilascio'), write the release date plus that period. Leave null if neither an expiry nor a validity period is printed on the certificate.",
      "title": "Data Scadenza"
    }
  },
  "title": "CertificateSchema",
  "type": "object"
}

IMPORTANT: All dates MUST be in ISO 8601 format (YYYY-MM-DD).

IMPORTANT EXTRACTION RULES FOR TRAINING CERTIFICATES:
- Training certificates vary widely in format (no national standard, regional agreements)
- 'tipologia_corso': Extract the course type/content found below the title (e.g., 'Addetto ai lavori in quota', 'utilizzo dei DPI di 3° categoria', 'Aggiornamento Preposto')
- 'numero_ore': Extract the number of training hours
- 'nome_persona': Extract the name of the person who attended
- 'data_emissione': Issue date — look for 'rilasciato il:' or the 'Data,' line near the signature at the bottom
- 'data_completamento_corso': Course completion date — look for 'Periodo di svolgimento del corso', 'Data fine corso', 'completato il'. This is the date the course was held, NOT the expiry.
- 'data_scadenza': ONLY set this if an explicit expiry is printed on the document. Acceptable triggers: 'valido fino a:', 'scadenza:', 'data di scadenza:', 'expires on'.
  * DO NOT use 'Periodo di svolgimento del corso', 'data emissione', 'rilasciato il', or any course completion date as the expiry.
  * If the document does NOT state an explicit expiry, leave data_scadenza null. A 5-year validity may apply by law, but it must be computed downstream — do not invent it here.

MULTI-PAGE HANDLING:
- If the document has multiple pages, later pages may contain legal communications (comunicazioni, interpelli, chiarimenti) that OVERRIDE the expiry date on the certificate.
- Example: a certificate says 'valido fino al 09/03/2025' but an attached legal communication clarifies that the update cycle is 5 years (quinquennale), making the real expiry 09/03/2028.
- If such a communication is present, compute the CORRECTED expiry date based on the issue date + the legally mandated update period, and use THAT as 'data_scadenza'.

Respond ONLY with the JSON, without additional text.

